    <content>
        <description>
            <levelledPara>
                <para>The Stratos propulsion system consists of two brushless DC electric motors
                    mounted on nacelles at the wing tips in a counter-rotating configuration.
                    Counter-rotation cancels the gyroscopic torque that a single motor would impose
                    on the airframe, improving directional stability during climb and
                    descent.</para>
            </levelledPara>
            <levelledPara>
                <para>Each motor is controlled by a dedicated electronic speed controller (ESC). The
                    ESCs receive pulse-width modulation signals from the flight controller and
                    regulate motor speed independently, which enables differential thrust for roll
                    control at low airspeeds.</para>
            </levelledPara>
            <levelledPara>
                <para>The propellers are folding two-blade composite units, 9 inches in diameter.
                    The folding mechanism allows the propellers to retract against the nacelle
                    during launch and automatically unfold under centrifugal force when the motors
                    reach operating speed.</para>
            </levelledPara>
        </description>
